cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GeoPotential — spatial multicriteria decision analysis for
  geoscientific data
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite the
  paper that describes the method. Cite the software itself as
  well when the implementation, and not only the method, is what
  your result depends on.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: do Amaral
    given-names: M. L. A.
    alias: marcuslucamaral
repository-code: https://github.com/marcuslucamaral/GeoPotential
abstract: >-
  A local-first desktop application for spatial multicriteria
  decision analysis. It loads vector, raster and tabular layers,
  brings them onto one analysis grid, converts each into a
  dimensionless suitability membership, and aggregates them into
  a prospectivity map by the Gamma fuzzy operator or by
  AHP-weighted linear combination. Every completed run writes a
  manifest that reproduces it: input checksums, CRS, grid,
  per-layer method and parameters, aggregation parameters and
  package versions.
keywords:
  - multicriteria decision analysis
  - MCDA
  - fuzzy logic
  - analytic hierarchy process
  - geographic information system
  - potential field
  - geothermal
  - mineral prospectivity
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
